From ab5d76e3ec4d8d83a74bcd2aa13224ab739a54fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Italicninja <dev@italicninja.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:46:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mod-forge core hooks: runtime item templates, an
 item-template load hook, talent rank bonuses

What mod-forge (https://github.com/italicninja/mod-forge) needs from the core. Nothing here knows about any one module.

- ObjectMgr::SetGeneratedItemTemplateLookup: GetItemTemplate falls through to it for entries item_template
  doesn't have. IsGeneratedItem: the entry is the lookup's, not item_template's.
- WorldScript::OnAfterItemTemplatesLoad, right after item templates and item set names, before auctions,
  guilds, mail and logins (they delete items whose template is missing).
- Null checks on the template where a generated entry can be gone once nothing holds it: Player::_SaveInventory
  and the loot packet.
- Player::SetTalentRankBonus(talentId, bonus): +ranks to a talent from outside the talent tree. The talent works
  at spent + bonus ranks (its auras' amounts and proc chance); a talent with no points spent is granted at the
  bonus. The talent tree the client shows never changes.
